Rāma asks why Bharata came in ascetic dress --- Bharata reports Daśaratha's heaven and Kaikeyī's sin --- Bharata begs Rāma to consecrate himself and save all --- Bharata clasps Rāma's feet weeping --- Rāma embraces Bharata and finds no fault --- Rāma forbids blaming his mother --- Rāma divides commands between kingdom and forest --- Rāma prizes his father's word above overlordship